<h2 class="bde-heading-390-188 bde-heading">
Hornets Payroll Questions Answered
</h2><div class="bde-shortcode-390-189 bde-shortcode"><div class="nst nst-component-faq" style="--nst-accent:#1D1160"><details class="nst-accordion"><summary>Who Is the Highest-Paid Player on the Charlotte Hornets?</summary><p>Coby White has the largest current cap hit at $26,811,593. His listed cash salary is $26,811,593.</p></details><details class="nst-accordion"><summary>What Is the Charlotte Hornets Payroll?</summary><p>The active roster cap payroll is $161,691,873 for 2026–27 in the 2026-10-21 snapshot. Dead cap and cap holds are separate.</p></details><details class="nst-accordion"><summary>How Much of the Salary Cap Does the Roster Use?</summary><p>Standard-roster cap charges equal 98.02% of the NBA’s $164,961,000 salary cap. This can exceed 100% because NBA rules allow certain exceptions.</p></details><details class="nst-accordion"><summary>Are Future Contract Totals Fully Guaranteed?</summary><p>No. Scheduled years can include player options, team options and conditional protection. The contract table identifies options where confirmed.</p></details><details class="nst-accordion"><summary>Why Are Salary and Cap Hit Different?</summary><p>Incentives, contract rules and minimum-salary adjustments can make a player’s cash pay differ from the amount charged to the team’s salary cap.</p></details><p class="nst-note"><a href="/methodology/">Research methodology</a> · <a href="/contact/">Report a correction</a></p><details class="nst-accordion"><summary>Data References</summary><ul><li><a href="https://www.spotrac.com/nba/charlotte-hornets/yearly">www.spotrac.com</a></li><li><a href="https://www.nba.com/news/nba-salary-cap-2026-27-season">www.nba.com</a></li><li><a href="https://www.nba.com/hornets/news/starting-from-scratch">www.nba.com</a></li><li><a href="https://www.nba.com/hornets/bobcats-sports-entertainment-applies-change-teams-name-hornets">www.nba.com</a></li><li><a href="https://jjnba.com/repeater/">Taxpayer history: JJNBA / Jeremiah Thomas · CC BY 4.0<