<script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/teams/charlotte-hornets/#faq","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/teams/charlotte-hornets/"},"mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Who is the highest-paid player on the Charlotte Hornets?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Coby White has the largest current cap hit at $26,811,593. His listed cash salary is $26,811,593."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the Charlotte Hornets payroll?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The active roster cap payroll is $161,691,873 for 2026–27 in the 2026-10-21 snapshot. Dead cap and cap holds are separate."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much of the salary cap does the roster use?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Standard-roster cap charges equal 98.02% of the NBA’s $164,961,000 salary cap. This can exceed 100% because NBA rules allow certain exceptions."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are future contract totals fully guaranteed?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Scheduled years can include player options, team options and conditional protection. The contract table identifies options where confirmed."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why are salary and cap hit different?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Incentives, contract rules and minimum-salary adjustments can make a player’s cash pay differ from the amount charged to the team’s salary cap."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How Does the Charlotte Hornets’ Payroll Compare With Southeast Rivals?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Explore the other Southeast Division teams and compare the contracts behind their payrolls."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How Much Are the Hornets Paying in Total Salary?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Charlotte Hornets salaries for 2026–27 add up to a cap payroll of $170.73 million, putting the club $5.77 million above the $164.96 million salary cap. That figure includes $9.04 million in dead cap for Rob Dillingham and Ryan Nembhard, both waived in September, on top of a standard roster of $161.69 million. Coby White tops the payroll at $26.81 million, ahead of Naz Reid on $23.28 million and Grayson Allen on $18.13 million, together about 42.2% of the roster total. Their tax salary is $29.70 million below the $200.43 million luxury-tax line and apron salary sits $37.78 million under the $209.02 million first apron."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What does going over the tax line mean?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The luxury tax is an additional team expense. It rises in bands as tax salary moves above the threshold; teams with a recent history of paying tax can face higher repeater rates. The final bill depends on the season-end calculation."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What Do the Hornets Owe in Future Salary?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"What the Hornets owe in future salary is led by Brandon Miller, whose five-year extension, worth a reported $209 million, runs to 2031-32. Naz Reid’s $125.00 million agreement runs to 2029–30, Coby White is signed through 2028–29 at $74.00 million and Grayson Allen through 2027–28 at $70.00 million. Two contracts end after this season, Grant Williams and Moussa Diabaté, so most of the current payroll still carries forward. Hannes Steinbach and Christian Anderson are also on the books to 2029–30 on rookie money. For each player’s 2026–27 figure, see the full list of Charlotte Hornets salaries in the roster table."}}]}</script>
